From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sadatdaniel <sadatdaniel@yahoo.com>
Date: Fri, 5 Sep 2026 00:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: samsung: abox: do not treat every stream widget as a DAI

Kernel panic, reproducible, as soon as a playback route to the speaker
amplifier is enabled and a stream is started:

  speaker-test: Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at
                virtual address 00000010
  pc : abox_hw_params_fixup_helper+0x830/0x1150
  lr : abox_hw_params_fixup_helper+0x804/0x1150
  Kernel panic - not syncing: Fatal exception

0x10 is offsetof(struct snd_soc_dai, dev) - name, id, dev - and
abox_if_hw_params_fixup_by_dai() opens with `struct device *dev =
dai->dev`.

The fallback branch of abox_hw_params_fixup_helper() walks a DAPM widget
list looking for the interface that should dictate the stream format:

	list_for_each_entry(w, &widget_list, work_list) {
		struct snd_soc_dai *dai;

		if (!w->sname)
			continue;

		dai = w->priv;
		if (abox_if_hw_params_fixup_by_dai(dai, params, stream) >= 0) {

but w->priv only holds a snd_soc_dai for DAI widgets - soc-dapm.c assigns
it in snd_soc_dapm_new_dai_widgets() and nowhere else. w->sname is set on
far more than that, AIF widgets included, so the loop hands
abox_if_hw_params_fixup_by_dai() a pointer that is not a DAI and it
dereferences it.

Guard it exactly the way ASoC's own snd_soc_dapm_connect_dai_link_widgets()
guards the identical lookup: filter on w->id being snd_soc_dapm_dai_in or
snd_soc_dapm_dai_out, then check w->priv is set at all. Also make
abox_if_hw_params_fixup_by_dai() reject a NULL dai rather than trust its
callers - it is already written to be called speculatively and to reject
DAIs that are not its own (`dev->driver != &samsung_abox_if_driver.driver`
-> -EINVAL), so a NULL dai returning -EINVAL fits that contract.

Why stock Android never hits this: the branch above is only reached when
the first attempt, abox_if_hw_params_fixup(rtd, params, stream) on
rtd->cpu_dai, fails. In Samsung's own configuration it succeeds, so the
fallback is dead code there. It is reached here because the route in use
puts the interface somewhere other than the runtime's own cpu_dai.

Not a local regression: the same unguarded loop and the same unguarded
abox_if_hw_params_fixup_by_dai() are present verbatim in other Samsung
Exynos ABOX trees (checked against the Galaxy Note9 exynos9810 Pie tree,
freeza-inc/bm-galaxy-note9-exynos-pie), so this is long-standing in
Samsung's driver rather than something this port introduced.

Found on a Galaxy A50 (exynos9610) running Ubuntu Touch, with the ABOX
DSP booting for the first time - see a50-ubuntu-touch
docs/experiments/007-abox-firmware-too-early.md. The panic is only
reachable once the DSP actually runs, which is why it had never been seen
on this device before.
---
diff --git a/sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox.c b/sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox.c
index 0d900fb0b..62e4b00d8 100644
--- a/sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox.c
+++ b/sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox.c
@@ -3288,10 +3288,31 @@ skip_capture:
 		list_for_each_entry(w, &widget_list, work_list) {
 			struct snd_soc_dai *dai;
 
+			/*
+			 * w->priv only holds a snd_soc_dai for DAI widgets -
+			 * soc-dapm.c sets it in snd_soc_dapm_new_dai_widgets()
+			 * and nowhere else. Every widget with a stream name
+			 * reaches this loop though, AIF widgets included, and
+			 * for those w->priv is not a DAI at all. Guard it the
+			 * way ASoC's own snd_soc_dapm_connect_dai_link_widgets()
+			 * does, or abox_if_hw_params_fixup_by_dai() dereferences
+			 * a non-DAI pointer at dai->dev.
+			 */
+			switch (w->id) {
+			case snd_soc_dapm_dai_in:
+			case snd_soc_dapm_dai_out:
+				break;
+			default:
+				continue;
+			}
+
 			if (!w->sname)
 				continue;
 
 			dai = w->priv;
+			if (!dai)
+				continue;
+
 			if (abox_if_hw_params_fixup_by_dai(dai, params, stream)
 					>= 0) {
 				abox_set_sif_auto_config(data, msg_rate, true);
diff --git a/sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox_if.c b/sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox_if.c
index 3a58f7f3a..3cd4e40be 100644
--- a/sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox_if.c
+++ b/sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox_if.c
@@ -911,11 +911,18 @@ module_platform_driver(samsung_abox_if_driver);
 int abox_if_hw_params_fixup_by_dai(struct snd_soc_dai *dai,
 		struct snd_pcm_hw_params *params, int stream)
 {
-	struct device *dev = dai->dev;
-	struct abox_if_data *data = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+	struct device *dev;
+	struct abox_if_data *data;
 	unsigned int rate, channels, width;
 	int ret = 0;
 
+	/* callers walk DAPM widget lists; not every widget carries a DAI */
+	if (!dai)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	dev = dai->dev;
+	data = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
 	if (dev->driver != &samsung_abox_if_driver.driver)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
-- 
2.43.0
